WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.642
An empty pivot cell should not automatically become zero.

00:00:03.642 --> 00:00:07.182
NULL may mean no observation was recorded.

00:00:07.182 --> 00:00:12.327
Zero may mean the observation exists and its measured value is zero.

00:00:12.327 --> 00:00:14.332
Those are different facts.

00:00:14.332 --> 00:00:21.727
Before using ELSE zero or COALESCE, decide what an absent source row means for the analytical question.

00:00:21.727 --> 00:00:26.772
After reshaping, NULL and zero may have very different meanings.

00:00:26.772 --> 00:00:31.322
NULL can mean the category did not occur or was not measured; zero can mean it was measured and the value

00:00:31.322 --> 00:00:40.160
was truly zero. Do not replace NULL with zero unless that interpretation is correct for the business question.
